#: ../../source/extending/common.rst:3
msgid "Replacing Common Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/common.rst:5
msgid ""
"There are quite a few functions necessary to CodeIgniter that need to be "
"loaded early for use in the core classes and thus cannot be placed into a"
" helper. While most users will never have any need to do this, but the "
"option to replace these functions does exist for those who would like to "
"significantly alter the CodeIgniter core. In the **app/** directory there"
" is a file **Common.php**, and any functions defined in there will take "
"precedence over the versions found in **system/Common.php**. This is also"
" an opportunity to create globally-available functions you intend to use "
"throughout the framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/extending/common.rst:12
msgid ""
"Messing with a core system class has a lot of implications, so make sure "
"you know what you are doing before attempting it."
msgstr ""

